Cornwall GP example: data/cornwall_*.rda, inst/extdata/cornwall_*
------------------------------------------------------------------
Built by data-raw/cornwall_gp.R from the sources below, subset to NHS
Cornwall and Isles of Scilly Integrated Care Board (QT6) and its 337 LSOA
2021 areas, joined on practice and LSOA codes and reprojected as needed.

GP registrations and workforce (cornwall_gp, cornwall_lsoa, cornwall_flows):
Patients Registered at a GP Practice (July 2026) and General Practice
Workforce (30 June 2026). Copyright (c) 2026 NHS England. Contains public
sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0,
https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/.

Small-area boundaries, population-weighted centroids and population
(cornwall_lsoa): Source: Office for National Statistics licensed under the
Open Government Licence v3.0 (LSOA 2021 boundaries with rural-urban
classification, LSOA 2021 population-weighted centroids, mid-2024 small area
population estimates via Nomis). Contains OS data (c) Crown copyright and
database right 2025.

Practice locations (cornwall_gp): ONS Postcode Directory, November 2025.
Contains OS data (c) Crown copyright and database right 2025. Contains Royal
Mail data (c) Royal Mail copyright and database right 2025. Source: Office
for National Statistics licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.

Population grid (cornwall_pop.tif): WorldPop (www.worldpop.org) and the
Center for International Earth Science Information Network (CIESIN),
Columbia University (2018). Global High Resolution Population Denominators
Project, 2020 UN-adjusted 1 km estimates for the United Kingdom,
https://doi.org/10.5258/SOTON/WP00671. Licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Modifications: cropped to the
area and weighted by the share of each cell inside it.

Travel times (cornwall_travel, cornwall_gp_travel.tif): derived by the
package author from the Malaria Atlas Project 2019 global motorised friction
surface (Weiss D.J. et al. (2020) Global maps of travel time to healthcare
facilities. Nature Medicine 26, 1835-1838,
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41591-020-1059-1) with least-cost paths over land,
from the practice and centroid locations above. The Malaria Atlas Project
publishes its maps under Creative Commons Attribution; its website states
version 3.0 and the Google Earth Engine catalogue entry states version 4.0.
The version applying to the downloaded surface has not been confirmed.


Administrative boundaries: data/bound0.rda, data/bound1.rda
------------------------------------------------------------
Source: Thailand administrative level 1 boundaries (file
tha_admbnda_adm1_rtsd_20220121, published 2022-01-21), Royal Thai Survey
Department (RTSD), distributed by UN OCHA as a Common Operational Dataset
(COD-AB), originally through the COD/FOD Registry on
HumanitarianResponse.info and now through the Humanitarian Data Exchange,
https://data.humdata.org/dataset/cod-ab-tha.
Modifications: subset to Health Region 12, selected columns, reprojected to
EPSG:32647; bound0 is the dissolved outer boundary of bound1.
Licence: the current HDX listing of this dataset is licensed under Creative
Commons Attribution for Intergovernmental Organisations 3.0 (CC BY-IGO 3.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/igo/. The metadata embedded in
the 2022 release used here refer instead to the COD/FOD Registry terms of use.


Under-five population: inst/extdata/u5pd.tif
--------------------------------------------
Source: Meta Data for Good and the Center for International Earth Science
Information Network (CIESIN), Columbia University, High Resolution
Population Density Maps, Thailand, children under five, 2020, downloaded
from the Humanitarian Data Exchange,
https://data.humdata.org/dataset/thailand-high-resolution-population-density-maps-demographic-estimates.
Source imagery (c) 2016 Maxar.
Modifications: aggregated by summation (factor 17.5), reprojected to
EPSG:32647 on a 520.4038 m grid by bilinear resampling (cell values are
therefore approximate counts), cropped and masked to Health Region 12.
Licence: listed on HDX as Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY), without a
version; Meta's current distribution of these maps states CC BY 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. The licence version of the
downloaded file has not been confirmed.


Health facilities: data/hc12_hos.rda, data/hc12_phc.rda
-------------------------------------------------------
Source: Office of the Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Public Health
(Thailand), Government Open Data Services, https://opendata.moph.go.th;
preparation script dated 2024-12-19. Facility GIS points, provider and
service-population statistics were requested for B.E. 2563, and
health-volunteer statistics, as written, for B.E. 2565. API responses were
not archived.
Modifications: subset to Health Region 12, joined across endpoints,
facility identifiers recoded, reprojected to EPSG:32647. Coordinates are
exact; the recoded identifiers are not an anonymisation.
Licence: redistribution terms for these data have not been confirmed.


Travel-time layers: data/hos_iscvec.rda, inst/extdata/hos_iscr.tif,
inst/extdata/phc_iscr.tif (and their *_names.rds companions)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Source: computed by the package author with OSRM (Open Source Routing
Machine) on a 2024 Geofabrik OpenStreetMap extract for Thailand, routed in
December 2024, from the facility locations in hc12_hos and hc12_phc. Each
layer stores travel-time band midpoints in minutes: hospital layers cover
bands up to 180 minutes; primary health centre layers are cut at 60 minutes.
NA marks cells outside the region or beyond the last band.
Map data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database
License (ODbL) 1.0, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright and
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/.
These layers are derived from OpenStreetMap data and from the Ministry of
Public Health facility locations above; their licence status has not been
finally determined. Until it is determined, users should assume that the
OpenStreetMap attribution and ODbL 1.0 obligations may apply, together with
any terms governing the facility data. This notice is not a licence grant
for these layers.
